===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|fa|چادر|tr=čâdor}}, from {{bor|en|sa|छत्त्र}}.<ref>[http://www.bartleby.com/61/28/C0222800.html Chador in the American Heritage Dictionary of the English Language]</ref>

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[loose]] [[robe]], made from a single [[cloth]], worn as a [[combination]] [[head]] [[covering]], [[veil]] and [[shawl]] by [[Muslim]] [[women]], especially in [[Iran]].

